+# Masiha sales bot
+Custom Python commerce engine and Telegram polling worker, native React administration and authenticated Go bridge. No WizWiz source is used.
+Panel route: /panel/sales-bot. POST /panel/api/sales-bot inherits panel authentication, token scope and CSRF.
+Private state: /etc/masiha-vpn-extension/sales/sales.db (root only). Never commit this database.
+Token is omitted from reads; an empty token field preserves the saved token. Disabled by default.
+Runtime: sales_worker.py supervised by the existing VPN worker/systemd cgroup. No extra public port or webhook.
+Configure BotFather token and numeric admin IDs in the panel; save, check connection, create plans, configure payment instructions, then enable.
+The bot must have no existing webhook or other polling process. Admins must start the bot to receive messages.
+
+Implemented:
+- Plan/category editing, capacity, existing Xray inbound selection, OpenVPN/OpenConnect time plans.
+- Wallet ledger, one-time order references, immutable expiring quotes, manual receipt approval, transfer.
+- Purchase, renewal, profile delivery, Xray subscription/direct links and locally generated QR.
+- One trial per Telegram account, gift/discount codes, referral commission.
+- Reseller discount and batch purchase, client display names, Xray credential/subscription rotation.
+- Forced channel membership and contact ownership checking.
+- Support tickets/replies, broadcast queue, admin notifications and report channel.
+- Expiry warnings and Xray traffic warning (currently first 100 active recorded services per sweep).
+- Account blocking, credit adjustments, orders needing review and retry.
+- Pending fulfillment preserves an absolute target before external operations; uncertain failures require admin review.
+- No automatic refunds after uncertain partial provisioning.
+- Telegram outbox delivery is at-least-once: a crash after Telegram accepts a message but before local acknowledgement may duplicate a notification, never a debit.
+
+Not yet implemented (do not advertise parity with every WizWiz feature):
+- NextPay and cryptocurrency gateways. Zarinpal request/verification and public return route are implemented; real merchant payment is not tested.
+- Automatic server health/failover, cross-server relocation, multi-panel sales and dedicated inbound creation.
+- Imported external subscription ownership verification and migration.
+- Custom volume/time add-ons separate from renewal, arbitrary custom button designer, scheduled broadcast UI.
+- OpenVPN/OpenConnect byte quota enforcement; time-only plans are validated.
+- Remote backup delivery through the bot.
+
+Verification:
+test_sales.py: money/ownership/duplicate orders, token omission, quotes and bulk buying.
+Frontend tests: JSON requests and numeric admin IDs.
+smoke_panel.py: isolated panel login, CSRF/auth rejection and settings page.
+Real provision/renew/delete tested using disposable accounts on all three adapters.
+Telegram live messaging remains untested until the operator supplies a token; no credentials are prepopulated.
+Preserve the custom source branch when updating upstream panel binaries.
+
+Zarinpal: https://www.zarinpal.com/docs/paymentGateway/connectToGateway
+Amounts stored as integer tomans and sent as integer IRR (times 10). Browser status does not credit; server verifies authority and stored amount. Duplicate 100/101 responses are protected by a unique ledger reference. The callback path /xui/sales-payment has bounded concurrent verification slots and does not accept arbitrary admin actions.
